# The deployed artifact is site/dist. This file controls what reaches the BUILD,
# which is a different question from what is served -- outputDirectory settles
# that -- so the only things excluded here are things the build must not have.
#
# The harness is one of them. It talks to a paid API with a key read from the
# environment, and none of it belongs on a static host. Its pyproject.toml is
# also what made Vercel try to deploy src/tee/cli.py as a Python function:
# excluding it leaves the detection nothing to find.
#
# Every pattern is anchored with a leading slash. Unanchored, `src/` matches at
# any depth and would take site/src -- the React app -- with it.
/pyproject.toml
/uv.lock
/src/
/tests/
/configs/
/corpora/
/fixtures/
/results/
/.tee/
/.venv/
/.pytest_cache/

# Reinstalled by `npm ci` anyway.
/site/node_modules/

# Nothing else under site/ is excluded. `build:ci` runs site/scripts/ for its
# checks, so excluding them as "sources, not served" broke the build -- and it
# bought nothing, since only site/dist is ever served.
